     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nAcetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6 g/day. That's well above the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day, and some institutions cap it at 3 g/day. The 2000 mg single dose is also twice the usual maximum of 1000 mg. At 6 g/day, even with normal liver function, there's a real risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options, depending on what you intended:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day). This is a common standard order.\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day). This is the usual maximum.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day).\n\nIf you meant something else, such as 2000 mg/day total, or if there's a reason for this dose, tell me and I'll enter it. Once you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll place the order right away."
      }
